  "name": "Back up workflows daily to GitHub with incremental updates",
  "active": false,
  "isArchived": false,
  "nodes": [
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Daily n8n Workflow Backup to GitHub\n\nThis workflow automatically backs up every workflow in your n8n instance to a GitHub repository once a day. It is smart: it only creates a file for a new workflow, and for an existing backup it updates the file only when the workflow actually changed — so your commit history stays clean.\n\n## How it works\n1. **Schedule Trigger** runs once a day at 11 PM\n2. **Get many workflows** lists every workflow in your n8n instance via the n8n API\n3. **Loop Over Items** processes one workflow at a time\n4. **Get a file** tries to read that workflow's existing backup file from GitHub\n5. **If** checks whether a backup already exists:\n   - **Not found** → **Get a workflow** (fetch full JSON) → **Create a file** on GitHub → **Wait** (rate limit)\n   - **Found** → **Get Last Update Date** (latest GitHub commit) → **filter_date** compares dates:\n     - n8n version is newer → **Download workflow** → **Edit a file** on GitHub → **Wait1**\n     - no change → **Wait2** (skip, no commit)\n6. The Wait nodes (10 seconds each) protect against GitHub API rate limits\n\n## Set up steps\n1. **n8n API** — create an n8n API key (Settings → n8n API) and connect it as the n8n credential in the three n8n nodes (Get many workflows, Get a workflow, Download workflow)\n2. **GitHub** — connect a GitHub credential (Personal Access Token with repo scope) in the four GitHub nodes\n3. **Repository** — replace `YOUR_GITHUB_USERNAME` and `YOUR_BACKUP_REPO` in the GitHub nodes (Create a file, Get a file, Edit a file, and the commits URL in Get Last Update Date) with your own GitHub username and the repo where backups should be stored\n4. Create an empty folder named `workflows` in that repo (or let the first run create files there)\n5. Activate the workflow. It will back up everything nightly at 11 PM",
        "height": 1020,
        "width": 560,
        "color": 4
      },
      "id": "75725220-ea82-44d0-a1db-20531b0f2886",
      "name": "Overview",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        368,
        240
      ],
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Trigger and List Workflows\nRuns daily at 11 PM, lists every workflow in your n8n instance, and loops over them one at a time.",
        "height": 190,
        "width": 540,
        "color": 5
      },
      "id": "ab63b16c-bfba-4512-9f19-b0df6583bcfb",
      "name": "Section — Trigger and List",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        976,
        240
      ],
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Check If Backup Exists\nTries to read the workflow's existing file from GitHub. The If node routes to create-new or update-existing based on whether a file was found.",
        "height": 190,
        "width": 340,
        "color": 6
      },
      "id": "c51806b8-e8d3-4506-97c1-2ad37237231d",
      "name": "Section — Check Exists",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        1584,
        240
      ],
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Existing Backup — Update Only If Changed\nGets the last GitHub commit date and compares it with the workflow's n8n updatedAt. If n8n is newer, it downloads the full workflow and updates the file. If nothing changed, it waits and skips (no commit). Wait nodes protect the GitHub rate limit.",
        "height": 190,
        "width": 1120,
        "color": 6
      },
      "id": "60108fd0-aaff-44e4-83e3-9b7930f92f74",
      "name": "Section — Update If Changed",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        1968,
        240
      ],
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## New Workflow — Create Backup\nFor a workflow with no existing backup, fetches the full JSON and creates a new file in the GitHub repo, then waits before the next loop.",
        "height": 190,
        "width": 480,
        "color": 5
      },
      "id": "63684870-854b-46a1-b2db-6261c42185e2",
      "name": "Section — Create New Backup",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        3136,
        240
      ],
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "\n\n\n\n## ⚠️ Setup Notes\n1. Credentials — replace both the n8n API credential (three n8n nodes) and the GitHub credential (four GitHub nodes) with your own. The GitHub token needs repo scope.\n2. Repository — set `YOUR_GITHUB_USERNAME` and `YOUR_BACKUP_REPO` everywhere they appear, including the commits URL in Get Last Update Date.\n3. Rate limits — the three Wait nodes (10 seconds) space out GitHub API calls. If you have hundreds of workflows, increase the wait or the schedule window.\n4. First run — on the very first run every workflow is created as a new file. After that, only changed workflows produce new commits.",
        "height": 570,
        "width": 380,
        "color": 3
      },
      "id": "f254fdeb-9042-4d87-949f-cf19ebbc922d",
